#: source/release-notes/rl-2.8.md:1
msgid "Release 2.8 (2022-04-19)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.8.md:3
msgid ""
"New experimental command: `nix fmt`, which applies a formatter defined by "
"the `formatter.<system>` flake output to the Nix expressions in a flake."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.8.md:7
msgid ""
"Various Nix commands can now read expressions from standard input using `--"
"file -`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.8.md:10
msgid ""
"New experimental builtin function `builtins.fetchClosure` that copies a "
"closure from a binary cache at evaluation time and rewrites it to content-"
"addressed form (if it isn't already). Like `builtins.storePath`, this allows "
"importing pre-built store paths; the difference is that it doesn't require "
"the user to configure binary caches and trusted public keys."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.8.md:17
msgid ""
"This function is only available if you enable the experimental feature "
"`fetch-closure`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.8.md:20
msgid ""
"New experimental feature: _impure derivations_. These are derivations that "
"can produce a different result every time they're built. Here is an example:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.8.md:24
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"stdenv.mkDerivation {\n"
"  name = \"impure\";\n"
"  __impure = true; # marks this derivation as impure\n"
"  buildCommand = \"date > $out\";\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.8.md:32
msgid ""
"Running `nix build` twice on this expression will build the derivation "
"twice, producing two different content-addressed store paths. Like fixed-"
"output derivations, impure derivations have access to the network. Only "
"fixed-output derivations and impure derivations can depend on an impure "
"derivation."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.8.md:38
msgid ""
"`nix store make-content-addressable` has been renamed to `nix store make-"
"content-addressed`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.8.md:41
msgid ""
"The `nixosModule` flake output attribute has been renamed consistent with "
"the `.default` renames in Nix 2.7."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.8.md:44
msgid "`nixosModule` → `nixosModules.default`"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.8.md:46
msgid ""
"As before, the old output will continue to work, but `nix flake check` will "
"issue a warning about it."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.8.md:49
msgid ""
"`nix run` is now stricter in what it accepts: members of the `apps` flake "
"output are now required to be apps (as defined in [the manual](https://nix."
"dev/manual/nix/stable/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-run.html#apps)), and members "
"of `packages` or `legacyPackages` must be derivations (not apps)."
msgstr ""
